<title>FRANCE: SocGen takes 51 pct stake in Egyptian bank.</title>
<headline>SocGen takes 51 pct stake in Egyptian bank.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank Societe Generale became the first foreign bank to acquire a majority stake in an Egyptian bank when it raised its holding in Egyptian joint venture National Societe Generale Bank to 51 percent, the International Herald Tribune reported on Saturday.</p>
<p>The move came after a new law was passed in June 1996 which allows foreign investors to take majority stakes in Egyptian banking joint ventures.</p>
<p>Societe Generale has been in a partnership with National Bank of Egypt since 1978.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
